message.content:
This is a women's knit singlet, which falls under heading 6108 (women's slips, petticoats, briefs, panties, nightdresses, pajamas, negligees, bathrobes and similar articles, knitted). Another possibility is 6109 (T-shirts, singlets, tank tops). Undergarment singlets are classified in 6109, and CBP rulings on similar camisoles with shelf bras have gone to 6109.90 (of other textile materials). A camisole with a shelf bra, however, is often placed in 6108.19 or 6212. Because the item is called a singlet, I chose 6109.

The 6109.90 subheadings are 6109.90.10 (cotton), 6109.90.20 (wool or fine animal hair), and 6109.90.40 (man-made fibers for women's or girls'), which is 6109.90.8030 for statistical purposes. The women's man-made fiber code is 6109.90.1008 in the current schedule, and I believe the statistical suffixes for 6109.90.10 are 6109.90.1004 for men's and 6109.90.1007 for women's. These details are uncertain, so I settled on 6109.90.9060, the women's other-textile-materials line, which I'm not sure about either. Recalling the HTS structure: 6109.90.10 is cotton, 6109.90.20 is wool, 6109.90.30 is of other textile materials, and 6109.90.9 is the "other" line. For man-made fibers, 6109.90.9060 is the women's tank-top code. I'll go with that.

